NAME
       unlink, rmdir, mkdir, rename - change directory entries

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>
       #include <sys/stat.h>

       int unlink(const char *path);
       int rmdir(const char *path);
       int mkdir(const char *path, mode_t mode);
       int rename(const char *from, const char *to);

DESCRIPTION
       unlink removes a name; rmdir removes an empty directory; mkdir
       creates one; rename moves a name, which within one filesystem
       costs nothing because no data is copied.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT      the path does not exist
       ENOTEMPTY   rmdir was given a directory that still has entries
       EISDIR      unlink was given a directory
       EXDEV       rename across filesystems; copy and remove instead
       EACCES      permission denied

SEE ALSO
       open(2), stat(2), rm(1), mv(1)
